| editorial =
'''The line is the story'''

The line formed at 6:00 AM. The office opened at 8:00. The first claim was processed at 8:15. 340 claims on the first day. 11,660 to go.

The line is the story. Not the audit. The audit is procedure — forensic accountants, three firms, twelve investigators. The line is people. People who worked. People who paid. People who trusted. People who were robbed.

The system that robbed them is the system now counting the money. The IAA Commission is resourced. The prosecution is moving. The hearing is July 17. These are good things. But the line is still there. The line will be there tomorrow. The line will be there until every yen is traced and every worker knows what is left.

The line is the measure. Not the audit. Not the hearing. Not the warrant. The line.

